 "stability_across_3_runs": "worst per-query spread 0.0010 ms across three runs per mode after a discarded warmup run per mode; node and edge counts identical across all runs in both modes and the cross-build parity flag held on every cell. FLOOR HELD AT 0.005 on the standing rationale (0.2.10/0.2.11): three runs in one warm window under-sample cross-session jitter, and 0.005 is 2.5x the cross-session evidence (0.0020 spreads at 0.2.9; 0.002 control re-measure at 0.2.10). Seventh baseline of the 0.2.6 corpus epoch (c449542e, 30 corpora). Control top20_by_branch_count re-qualified across the kglite 0.16.15->0.16.17 engine move: the release-gate anchor compare vs 0.2.9 read it steady docs-off (+6.25%) and sub-floor docs-on (+0.003 ms raw under the 0.005 floor) \u2014 wandering, not deterministic (doctrine R11 corollary). Captured after the dep-debuginfo cap (line-tables-only) landed; the cap changes rlib bytes, not codegen of our release profile, and nodes/edges/query cells confirm it.",
